--- Part 2: fog colour behaviour in lava (isEyeInWater == 1) ---
  before tint 0.25   color = (0.1000, 0.0350, 0.0150)  luminance = 0.0474
  after  tint 0.50   color = (0.2000, 0.0700, 0.0300)  luminance = 0.0948
  Solas fogCol       color = (0.2460, 0.1869, 0.1572)  luminance = 0.1973
  note: Solas brightens via sqrt(sqrt(normalize(fogColor))); Astra's palette
        is used un-normalised and un-rooted, so the 0.25 was a darker colour
        than the reference it cites. 0.50 halves that gap without matching
        the reference's washed-out luminance (lava should still read dim).

--- Part 3: volume coefficients, 16-step radiative recurrence ---
  A faithful reduction of the march in nether_volume.glsl: d = (exp2-like
  sample distribution), step length = dd*dL, per-step transmittance
  exp(-density*steplen), plume absorbance multiplies the running transmittance
  and haze deliberately does not. Density inputs are held at one mid value so
  the before/after ratio is the only thing being measured:
    densityVol = 0.0996 (the mid-air ceiling at worldY 55: astra_bliss_cloud
      returns max((exp((100-y)/-15) - P^2(1-E))*2, ~0) = max(0.0996-..., 0), so no
      y=55 sample can exceed 0.0996), worldY = 55 (pow4 factor = 1),
    dL = 64 blocks, distance falloff pow5(1 - dist/borderFogDistance) applied.
  before  plume accumulated = 0.49110   haze = 0.00806   remaining transmittance = 0.5089
  after   plume accumulated = 0.49110   haze = 0.02416   remaining transmittance = 0.5089
  ceiling term uses the same shape with density 0.001*cube(y-40/50)*0.60*scale:
    before  density at y>=90 = 0.000210  (was the whole term below 1% of the
            medium colour? then it could not be seen)
    after   density at y>=90 = 0.000420  (was the whole term below 1% of the
            medium colour? then it could not be seen)

  reading: at the shipped coefficients the plume integrated over a 64-block ray
  already contributes 49.11% of the medium colour (transmittance falls to 0.509),
  so the plume IS the volume - it is not weak and is left unchanged. Haze sits at
  0.81% and the ceiling at 0.00021 density, i.e. below the level anything on
  screen can show; those two are the structural gap. The after values lift haze
  to 2.42% and ceiling to 0.00042 - the smallest values that can contribute -
  without touching the plume or approaching opacity.

